hadiths[75]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3197","On the authority of Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, Sayyidna Ali, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Zayd said: The father will pull the wala of his son (to himself)."
"3198","Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: Dada will pull Wala."
"3199","On the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, Qazi Shareeh said: The father will pull the veil of his son."
"3200","Narrated by Imam Amir Shaabi, may God have mercy on him: A slave dies and his free father and his sons (i.e. sons of the deceased) by a free woman are present, then for whom will it be? He said: In such a case, the villas owned by the grandfather will belong to him."
"3201","It was narrated from Mughirah that Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: A slave of Maktab died, who had paid half of the installments and had a son from his free wife. He said: I think he will take away his son's villa."
"3202","According to the ruling, Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: Qazi Shareeh did not refer to him when making a decision."
"3203","It was narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, said: If a slave has a free wife in marriage, his son will also be free with his mother, and when the father is freed, he will take away the wife."
"3204","It is said about a woman freed from Ata who is married to a slave: The children born to her during her slavery will belong to the benefactors of the woman, and the children born after the slave's freedom will belong to the people of the slave's blessings."
"3205","It was narrated from Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If a free woman is married to a slave and a boy is born to that slave, then the boy will be freed along with the freedom of his mother, and his walaa will be for the owners of his mother, then when the slave is freed, his walaa will go to his father's guardian"
"3206","On the authority of Alaa bin Abd al-Rahman, his father said: My mother was a freed slave of Haraqah (tribe) and my father was a slave of the schools of Yaqub Malik bin Aws bin Haddan Nasri, then my father paid the prescribed amount for the school, then Haraqi came to Sayyiduna Uthman R.A. At that time, Aws bin Malik was also sitting with him. is Both of them asked Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) for a decision, so he gave a decision in favor of Harqi, that is, he gave a decision in favor of the mother's follower, not in favor of the father's follower."
"3207","Suham bin Yazid Hamrawi reported that a man died and left no heir, he wrote about this to Umar bin Abdul Aziz who was the caliph at that time, he replied that his inheritance should be given to those who took wazifa with him, so under his supervision he divided his inheritance among those who took wazifa with him."
"3208","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A Muslim who has a will does not have the right to spend even two nights without having his will written down with him."""
"3209","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: A believer does not eat to his full stomach, and his will is always by his side."
"3210","It was narrated from Qasim bin Umar that Samamah bin Hazan said to me: What did your father do? I said: He passed away. He said: Did he make a will? Because it was said that when a person makes a will, his will makes up for what he lacked in Zakat. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Others have said Qasim bin Amr."
"3211","Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said: It is said that whoever makes a will that does not involve injustice, he will have the same reward as if he had given charity in his lifetime."
"3212","Narrated by Qazah: Haram ibn Hayyan was asked to make a bequest, so he said: I bequeath you the last verses of Surah Nahl, and Ibn Hayyan said these verses from ""I pray to your Lord with wisdom"" to ""And those who are good"". Read on."
"3213","Talha bin Barqul Al-Ilyami said: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfi, may Allah be pleased with him: Did the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, make a will? He replied: No, I asked: Then how is a will obligatory on people? Or why they were ordered to bequeath? He replied: This is (clear) from the Book of Allah Al-Qur'an, most probably the reference is ""Izza Hazara Ahadakum Al-Mawt"". . . . . .» [Baqarah: 180/2] is on the side. Huzail bin Shahrabeel said: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may God bless him and grant him peace) could rule over the will of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3214","From Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, ""If you leave a good will."" . . . . .» [Al-Baqarah: 180/2] It is narrated that ""good"" in this verse refers to wealth, which was said to be a thousand or more."
"3215","Abdullah bin Aun reported that Muhammad bin Sirin, may God have mercy on him, made a will and wrote: This is the mention of the will that he wrote, or he wrote: This is the mention of the will of Muhammad bin Sirin (Abu Bakr bin Abi Umrah) for his son and his family: Fear Allah, and mend mutual relations, and obey Allah and His Messenger if you are believers [Translation: Surah Al-Anfal: 1/8], then to them Bequeathed by Ibrahim (peace be upon him) to his sons and Jacob (peace be upon him): O my sons! Allah Ta'ala has chosen this religion for you, beware that you die as a Muslim [al-Baqarah 122/2], and bequeathed to them not to be disrespectful to the Ansar and their religious brothers, and that chastity and truth are better and purer than fornication and lying, if any accident happens to me due to this illness and I do not change this will, then he wrote the necessary things in the will."
"3216","It was narrated from Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: He used to make a will like this: This is the will of so-and-so, son of so-and-so, that he bears witness that there is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, I bear witness that Muhammad is the servant of Allah and His Messenger, and there is no doubt about it that the Hour will come, and Allah will resurrect those who are in the graves, and He will bring back to life those who are in the graves. He would bequeath them to fear Allah, and mend their mutual relations, and if they are believers, to obey Allah and His Messenger, and he would bequeath the same as Ibrahim (peace be upon him) bequeathed to his sons and Yaqub (peace be upon him): O my son! Allah Ta'ala has chosen the religion (Islam) for you, so you should die as a Muslim, then he willed that if any accident occurs in this disease, then his will is as follows......."
"3217","It was narrated from Hafs bin Ghailan that Makhool, may God have mercy on him, when he made his will, said: We bear witness to it, there is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, and Muhammad is His slave and messenger, and whoever believes in Allah and rejects idols, he will die and be raised on it, God willing. And they bequeathed about the leave given by Allah: if an accident happens to them, it should be done in this way if they do not exchange it (i.e. if they do not exchange it themselves before they die, then this will is enforceable)."
"3218","It was narrated from Makhool, may God have mercy on him, that this (above) will is of Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may God be pleased with him)."
"3219","Abu Hiyaan al-Taimi narrated from his father that Rabi bin Khatym wrote a will (as follows): Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim: This is the will of Rabi bin Khatym. And I bear witness, and the testimony of Allah is sufficient, Who bestows reward and reward on His righteous servants, I am satisfied with Allah as Lord and Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet, and I command myself and whoever obeys me to worship Allah with the worshipers, to praise Him among the praisers, and to wish good with the Muslim community."
"3220","Hisham narrated from his father that Sayyidna Ali (RA) went to a sick person and people mentioned his will, then Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: Allah said: (If he leaves wealth...) and I am of the opinion that he did not leave wealth. Hammad said: I remember he left more than seven hundred."
"3221","Hisham narrated from his father: Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib Radiyallahu Anhu went to visit a man of his tribe, so he said: Do I have to make a will? Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No, you are not leaving any wealth, leave your (little) wealth for your children."
"3222","Mansoor narrated from Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, that a man should make a will (more than a third) and his heirs should be witnesses and acknowledge it? Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: (Such a will) is not permissible. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This means that if he dislikes it later, such a will will not be enforced."
"3223","Shu'ba said: I asked Haqm and Hamad about the saints (heirs) that they allow a will and when (a person) dies, they do not accept a will? Both said: (It is) not permissible."
"3224","On the authority of Amir (Shaabi) may Allah have mercy on him, (Qadi) Shareeh said: If a man bequeaths more than one-third, if his heirs allow it, we will also allow it, and if the heirs say that we have allowed it, then they still have the right after giving the soil. (i.e. keep it if you want and reject it if you want)."
"3225","It is narrated from Qasim that a man asked his heirs to bequeath more than one-third, the heirs gave him permission, then after his death they withdrew the permission. (That is, it is not permissible to force more than one-third of the will)."
"3226","On the authority of Hisham, Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said about a man who bequeaths more than a third (third) and the heirs agree to it, he said: It is permissible. Imam al-Darmi Abu Muhammad, may God have mercy on him, said: It is permissible, but only during his life (not after death)."
"3227","Muhammad bin Sa'd (Ibn Abi Waqqas) narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him in Makkah. He had only one daughter. Sayyidna Sa'd (bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I asked him: I have only one daughter. Shall I bequeath all my wealth (for good deeds)? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No"". The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “No.” Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, one-third, although one-third is too much."""
"3228","Amir bin Sa'd narrated from his father (Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him) that I was with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Hajj, when he fell ill and was close to death. I understand that I will not be able to survive from this disease and I am very rich and I have no heir except a girl, should I donate all my wealth? He said: ""No"", I said: Then I give half of the wealth in charity? He said: ""No"", I said: Then should I give a third of my wealth in charity? He said: ""Yes, you can give one-third in charity."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One-third of wealth, even if one-third is too much. Indeed, if you leave your heirs rich, that is better than if you leave them poor and they go around begging in front of people, and whatever you spend, Allah will give you reward and reward until you get a reward for this morsel."" You will put it in your wife's mouth."""
"3229","It was narrated from Alaa bin Ziyad that Ziyad bin Matar made a will that my will is the one that the jurists of Basra agree on."
"3230","It was narrated on the authority of Alaa bin Ziyad that a man asked Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): My heir is Kalalah (no son), can I bequeath half of the property? Sayyiduna Umar said: No, he said: One third? He said: No, he said: A quarter? He said: No. He said: Of Khums (of the fifth part). He said: No, until he reached the tenth part."
"3231","Amir (Shaabi) may Allah have mercy on him said: People used to bequeath Khums and a quarter, and a third was the limit of prohibition. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Jami means disobedient self-headed horse."
"3232","Bakr (Ibn Abdullah Muzni) said: I made a will for Hameed bin Abd al-Rahman, so he said: I cannot accept the will of a man who has children and he bequeaths a third (i.e. a will of less than a third can be accepted)."
"3233","Qazi Shareeh said: Thulath (third part) is hard work but it is permissible."
"3234","On the authority of Mansur (Ibn al-Mu'tamar), Ibrahim (may God have mercy on him) said: The sixth part (for bequest) was dearer to the people than the third part."
"3235","It was narrated from Mughirah that Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: The testator is the trustee of that which is being bequeathed to him."
"3236","On the authority of Abu Wahhab, Makhool, may God have mercy on him, said: The case of the testator is permissible in everything except the house, shop, and land. If he sells anything, it will not be annulled. This is the opinion of Yahya bin Hamza."
"3237","Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: The executor is in charge of everything except freeing the slave, and he can establish a villa."
"3238","Mansoor (Ibn al-Mu'tamar) narrated that Ibrahim (may God have mercy on him) said: A testator (to whom a bequest has been made) will work (trade, etc.) in the property of an orphan when a man has bequeathed it to him."
"3239","It is narrated on the authority of Ismail that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: The bequest of an orphan will intercede for him, and the executor of a missing person to whom intercession has been bequeathed will also intercede."
"3240","Narrated by Ikrimah: A sheikh of Damascus said: I was with Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, and Sulaiman bin Habib and Abu Qalaba were also present, when suddenly a boy came and said that such and such a place is our land, which our executor sold for you. He answered roundly, then he turned to Abu Qalaba and said: What do you say? They said: Return the boy's land. They said: Then our property will be destroyed. He replied: You have wasted your own property."
"3241","On the authority of Ash'ath, Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said about a person who bequeathed half (of his property) to one man and a third of his (property) to another, Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Both of them will be given a share of the third (third), half to the one who has half and one-third to the one who has a third."
"3242","On the authority of al-Shaybani (Sulaiman bin Abi Sulaiman) Imam Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: The testator can change the will in whatever way he wants, except for freedom (there is no change in it)."
"3243","It was narrated on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Rabi'ah that Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: A man can add whatever he wants to his will, and the last will will be the original."
"3244","Amr bin Dinar narrated that his father freed his slave during his illness, then he felt that he should take them back (i.e. not free them) and free the other slaves, then those slaves quarreled with me in front of Abdul Malik bin Marwan, then Abdul Malik justified the freedom of the second party and revoked the freedom of the first ones."
"3245","On the authority of Sharid bin Suwayd, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A man can add whatever he wants to his will, and the last will is the original. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Hammam did not listen to Amr bin Shuaib and there is a Qatadah between them."
"3246","On the authority of Muammar, Imam Zuhri, may God have mercy on him, said about a person who makes a will, then makes another will? Al-Zuhari, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Both bequests are permissible in his own property (i.e. he has the right to exchange)."
"3247","It is narrated from Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The last will is the original."
"3248","Yahya said: When the judge accuses the testator, he should not separate him, but appoint someone else as a lawyer along with him. This is also the opinion of Uza'i. (This is also narrated from Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him)."
"3249","On the authority of Amir (Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him), he said: It is permissible to buy, sell and marry a sick person, and it will not be one-third."
"3250","Haris Akali said: What a sick person buys and sells during his illness will be one-third of his property with a reasonable price."
"3251","Yahya bin Saeed said: A woman of our family gave a donation while she was pregnant. Qasim (Ibn Muhammad may God bless him and grant him peace) was asked about it, and he said: That donation will be taken from the whole wealth, and Yahya said: We say that if a donation is given to her when the pain starts, it will be taken from a third of the wealth."
"3252","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) said about a person who said to his slave: If I enter the house of so-and-so, then my slave is free, then he also entered that house in a state of illness. Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: He will be freed from one-third of the wealth, and if he enters this house in a state of health, he will be freed from all the wealth."
"3253","Makhool (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If the heirs (of the deceased) are in need, then in my opinion there is no problem in giving them a share even of a third of the wealth."
"3254","Mugheera and Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: If two of the heirs testify (of the debt or bequest to the deceased), it will be valid for all the heirs, and if only one heir is a witness, then the payment (of the debt or will) will be made from his share and fortune."
"3255","Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, says: If one of the heirs gives testimony, the payment will be made from his share. Finally, he said: Payment will be made from the share of all the heirs."
"3256","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: When a man bequeaths one-third or one-fourth of his property, it will be paid from the fixed property and debt, and if he bequeaths from fifty-sixty to one hundred (i.e., less than one-third), then the bequest will be paid from the specified property until it is equal to one-third (i.e., one-third)."
"3257","Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qasit said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""A man has the right to spend one-third of his wealth wherever he wants."""
"3258","Abu Habiba said: I asked Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him: What is the ruling on a man who has dedicated his money in the cause of Allah? Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""The example of a person who gives charity or gives freedom at the time of his death is like that of a person who gives a gift after his stomach is full."""
"3259","Al-Hasan, may God have mercy on him, narrated: A man makes various wills, including the freeing of a slave, and if that will exceeds a third, then the slave will be freed first."
"3260","It was narrated from Muhammad (Ibn Sirin, may God have mercy on him) that the first parts will be divided."
"3261","If a man makes a will and frees (a slave) and there is an awl in his will (i.e. more shares), then this awl will be on all the freedmen and the bequest. Ata said: The people of Medina prevailed over us in this issue, they started with freedom."
"3262","Amr bin Dinar said: Whoever makes a bequest for freeing and any other bequest that is more than a third, the shares will be divided (out of the third)."
"3263","Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Whoever bequeaths more than a third of his wealth, including the freedom of a slave, he said: Freedom will come first."
"3264","Ibrahim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Liberation will be prioritized over will."
"3265","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: If a man makes a will for someone's children, then the wealthy, the needy, the male and the female will all be equal in this will. That is, everyone will be given an equal share of the third."
"3266","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: If a man makes a will for someone's children, then both men and women will be equal in it."
"3267","Siyar bin Abi Karb narrated that a man came to Qazi Shareeh and asked: A man should bequeath a part of his wealth, so he said: It will be included in the obligation, and a part of it for which the bequest is made will be given to him like other shares."
"3268","Makhool, may God have mercy on him, said: If a man in good health gives more than half of his wealth to an heir, then it should be limited to a third, and if he gives half of his wealth from himself, it will be permissible for him. Saeed said: The people of Damascus used to give fatwas for him."
"3269","Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: The cost of the shroud (of the deceased) will be from all the wealth of the deceased."
"3270","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: A man dies and leaves two thousand dirhams, and he owes that much or more. He said: This will provide for his burial, and the debt will not be paid."
"3271","Ibrahim, may God have mercy on him, said: In such a case, the beginning will be with the shroud, then the debt (from the child) will be paid, and after that the will will be enforced."
